{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Limits to Growth.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Limits to Growth.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"limits to growth limits to growth","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Limits to Growth.md","fileName":"Limits to Growth.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Limits to Growth","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[System Dynamics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["System Dynamics","Reinforcing Loop","Balancing Loop","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Limits to Growth.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Limits to Growth.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"limits to growth limits to growth","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Limits to Growth.md","fileName":"Limits to Growth.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Limits to Growth","heading":"Limits to Growth","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Limits to growth is a system pattern in which a [[Reinforcing Loop]] initially drives rapid expansion, but a limiting resource activates a [[Balancing Loop]]. Growth then slows into an S-shaped path or overshoots and crashes.\n\nThe pattern matters in progression and economy design because apparently stable growth can conceal a constraint that emerges only later. Recognizing the limiting stock or flow allows the designer to shape the transition intentionally.","tags":["baby"],"links":["System Dynamics","Reinforcing Loop","Balancing Loop","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Limits to Growth.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Limits to Growth.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"limits to growth limits to growth","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Limits to Growth.md","fileName":"Lim